  "perFamilyFindings": {
    "one-site-multiple-contacts-reachable-epitope": "Content matches affinity/avidity/accessibility. Defect: in panel 2 the teal connector between the two binders is drawn across the top of the first binder and its beige target, so link and shapes overlap. Panel 3 \"Hidden site\" arrow tip lands on the blocking shape, not clearly on the hidden epitope. Dark: contrast fine.",
    "binding-is-only-one-step-v2 (raster)": "Four scenes match lesson caption. Yellow burst marks beside the T-cell receptor tail in panel 4 read as signalling occurring, while the caption says no successful outcome is shown; panel 4 target is not clearly anchored on the target cell. Light/dark labels readable.",
    "one-binding-module-distinct-format-contexts": "Both: the second line of panel-1 caption touches the bottom edge of its card; \"Signaling\" label, arrow and caption crowd; neither membrane in the CAR panel is labelled target cell or T cell; the free-floating circle beside the soluble binder is unlabelled.",
    "scfv-vhh-linked-and-single-domains": "Both: \"binding face\" leader line strikes through the word \"face\"; the small chevron glyphs overlap the letters VH, VL and VHH. VH and VL are drawn apart, joined only by the linker, while the label says paired domains.",
    "selected-display-hit-sequence-and-testing": "Both: \"Rank -> make -> measure\" runs past the right edge of its card; \"A score is a prediction\" sits on the card bottom edge; the protein icon sits under Gene B while the label \"Make protein B\" is under Sequence B.",
    "resin-protection-coupling-and-release": "Both: panel-3 wash arrow points right, toward the chain, although the caption says soluble leftovers leave; the long repeat arrow on the right runs along and through card edges; after cleavage the connecting line is drawn through the three beads (strike-through look) unlike panels 1-3.",
    "old-new-lots-and-evidence-bridge-b10": "Both: subtitle \"Same starting material, if suitable\" collides with the top vial cap; \"Old process\" and \"New process\" labels crowd between vials; the alt text says paired lot vials lead to matched comparisons but no connector joins the vials to the comparison box.",
    "identity-activity-and-clinical-evidence": "Content consistent with lesson. Panel 3 has a large empty area; the product-plus-target versus target-only comparison shows no readout or control marks even though text says keep controls. No overlap defects seen."
  },
